Finally, after about 3 years of playing Hack in its various forms I won.
First there was 'Hack', from Fred Fish disk no. 7, played on a friend's
Amiga 1000 (which he didn't see again for ages). Then came Hack 1.0.3d in
COLOR, then HackLite, which I preferred to Nethack 2.3 (was all I could
get at the time.). Then Nethack 3.0j (played on lots of machines. PC,
Amiga, Sun, Vax). 
 
Anyway, Grue the Demigod ascended with about 1.1 million points and 2 wishes
left. I guess I should have wished for some dilithium but I didn't think
about it. Finding a ring shop with over 30 rings in it (including all the major
ones except teleport control) helped a lot. It turned out that teleport
control wasn't needed, the Wizard was sitting (very thoughtfully) right
under the castle. The only cheating involved was using some of that infinite
gold to get a -20 AC - I haven't seen a wand of polymorph in over 20 games.

